{"parentUuid":"1f0a5370-bba9-4794-aea6-9ae356933673","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_011CfpMcn5kW4nJcumqmsBqJ","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","stop_reason":"tool_use","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V6spn9L6bay8oTLfmc6fFZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/groom/e79.txt","content":"hands holds every dialog until one deadline, taken from the PermissionRequest hook's timeout (85 s), and warns the user 10 s before it (src/hands/core/reducer.py, src/hands/sessions/hookconfig.py). Claude Code has its own askUserQuestionTimeout setting; when it is shorter, Claude Code continues the question unanswered first ('No response after 60s — continued without an answer'), and the user is never told the question was about to be dropped. hands sees the end correctly (the dialog closes when the tool finishes); only the warning and the deadline are wrong for questions.\n\nSeen in the hands-tmux-510.0bj checkpoint run, 2026-10-06, with askUserQuestionTimeout \"60s\" in the user's Claude Code settings: an AskUserQuestion requested at 16:09:01.8Z was finished by Claude Code at 16:10:01.9Z with no deadline warning spoken. With --settings '{\"askUserQuestionTimeout\":\"10m\"}' the same question was warned at 75 s and let go at 85 s.\n\nDone when:\n- A question's warning is spoken before the session's own question timeout, whatever it is set to, and a question's deadline is never later than that timeout.\n- A test covers a question timeout shorter than the hook's (e.g. 60 s: warned before 60 s), and one where it is longer (warned and let go on the hook's deadline, as now).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2107}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"26826251-c486-4d64-8950-c85c4fb9ff11","timestamp":"2026-10-08T07:13:53.803Z"}
