{"parentUuid":"6880dba3-2b55-4f9c-a4b0-e87b0673200e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"38301ce5-954d-4b71-94e7-e9441d281c50","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"What about accessibility permissions? We will need that.  ensure that's accounted for\n\nThis should be a professional guided workflow like every paid app uses.  We do not demand any permissions when launching the app.  we show a window that explains in one short sentence that we need to ask for permissions for X functionality.  the user hits next, we request the functionality, the user can approve.  we do this with each permission until the flow is complete.  if a user hits no or exits,  we ask again, and the user recieves the popup again.  There is no requirement that users navigate anywhere and toggle things themselves.  We do it for them"},"uuid":"9db4e61f-b901-4975-934c-4b50b5f6eea0","timestamp":"2026-10-07T17:51:40.655Z"}
